# Prime Mentor Visual Design Law

DARK AURORA is the default Prime Mentor theme. Cream / off-white is not part of the brand.

## Default visual language

- Deep midnight navy, black-blue, cosmic gradients
- Aurora cyan, teal, restrained violet
- Gold accents and bright high-contrast type
- Premium translucent dark cards and subtle atmospheric glow
- Cosmic, sophisticated, mystical, premium, modern, readable

## Prohibited as a page theme

Do not use cream, ivory, warm off-white, pale beige, washed-out cream-to-blue gradients, or pastel shells as the dominant background.

Light colors are for text, icons, artwork, and isolated contrast only.

## When building or changing a page

1. Assume dark aurora. Reuse existing tokens, `PublicEnergyBackground`, cosmic/aurora CSS, gold/cyan accents, and glass/dark cards.
2. Never introduce a cream/off-white theme unless Brad explicitly requests it for that page.
3. Do not infer that a new landing page, webinar, product, course, report, or promotion should be light.
4. A white header is only for non-marketing/member chrome. Public marketing pages use the dark shared header. A white nav does not authorize a cream content shell.
5. Add new public marketing routes to `isMarketingSurface` in `apps/web/src/layouts/RootLayout.tsx` so they inherit `bg-[#04050f]`, the dark header, and `PublicEnergyBackground`.

## Review gate

Before marking a public page complete, ask: "Does this unmistakably look like The Prime Mentor?"

If it looks cream, beige, pastel, generic-light, or disconnected from dark aurora, the work is not complete.
